      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a comprehensive troubleshooting guide for VPN connection timeouts: \n\n1. Insure your VPN is regionally compatible with your device's browser; some VPNs may only work with select browsers, either due to security restrictions or authorizations.\n2. Restart your VPN by disconnecting then reconnecting, which usually resolves everyday connection issues if the server isn't servicing your region correctly.\n3. Your DNS settings might be complicit in a VPN timeout; most people know their local DNS as their router's default value. Change it to Google's server or try out a VPN's specific public DNS for mitigation.\n4. Not all VPNs use or offer superior mobile or desktop apps; switching might aid to get an adequate browser connection from your VPN.\n5. Be certain your firewalls aren't blocking your VPN traffic by temporarily disabling them and checking if a timeout persists on your own device before erring on the side of caution to call help desk.",
